# `plugin/bin/delulu` is `#!/bin/sh`. A CRLF checkout on Windows makes the shebang `/bin/sh\r`,
# which fails as "bad interpreter" — a broken install, not a line ending, as far as the user can
# tell. Its Windows twin has the opposite requirement: cmd.exe wants CRLF.
* text=auto
plugin/bin/delulu text eol=lf
plugin/hook/*.mjs text eol=lf
plugin/bin/*.cmd text eol=crlf

# esbuild output, 95KB and 46KB, regenerated by `npm run build` and byte-checked by shipped.test.ts.
# Marking them keeps them out of diffs by default and out of the repository language stats — the
# same invariant the CI workflow exists to protect, stated where GitHub reads it.
plugin/hook/handoff.mjs linguist-generated
plugin/hook/resume.mjs linguist-generated
